    "created_at": "2025-04-02T04:56:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-02T17:58:57Z",
    "body": "This would be great to have! But for those specifically looking for this for turning the kubernetes plugin on, may I suggest doing something like the following:\n\n```\n[kubernetes]\ndisabled = false\nformat = '[$symbol$context \\($namespace\\) $symbol]($style)'\ndetect_env_vars = [\"KUBIE_ACTIVE\"]\ndetect_files = [\"kubectx\"]\nstyle = 'blue bold'\n```\n\nIf you are on Linux or macOS, use kubie to switch your context and this plugin will automatically activate. Unfortunately, kubie doesn't work on Windows, so as a hack, I just cd into `~.\\kube` where a file called `kubectx` exists, so being in that directory activates the plugin.\n\nEDIT: After some additional testing you'll want to use either `detect_env_vars` OR `detect_files` as using both seems to not work on zsh on macOS (fine on PowerShell on Windows though).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
